.SS "double csmp::LinearLineElement::dN_AtNode (\fBDenseMatrix\fP< DM_MIN > & DN, uint32_t node)\fR [virtual]\fP"

.IP "1." 4
Pre-multiplies local interpolation function derivative matrix, B, with node coordinates to obtain the Jacobian matrix, J at the desired node point\&.
.IP "2." 4
The Jacobian matrix J is inverted and multiplied with B to obtain the global interpolation function derivative matrix at the point i (i=0\&.\&.\&.i=gauss points-1)\&.
.PP
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The first argument is a reference to the parent \fBElement\fP object, the second argument is the result matrix, the third argument indicates the gauss point at which the derivative matrix is computed and the fourth argument specifies the degrees of freedom per node, for which the B matrix shall be transformed\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The global interpolation function derivative matrix is returned into the second method argument\&. The method also returns the determinant of the Jacobian matrix since it is often needed in integration procedures\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Reimplemented from \fBcsmp::FiniteElement\fP\&.
